<p>
MyBigAdventure&trade; wishes to generate money for charity through ad revenue.  As a means to that end, MyBigAdventure&trade; has partnered with Google&trade; to provide all advertisement content.  All ads on this website originate from the Google&trade; AdSense Program, an impressive service that delivers high quality advertising based on website content.
<p>
My hope is the ads provide a value-added service to the visitorship, enabling easy access to products and services directly related to what the visitor is reading.  For example, the visitor is learning about my walk of the Fredom Trail in Boston, MA, and the ads posted along side my writeup relate to interests local to Boston such as hotels, restaurants, sights, airfare, etc.
<p>
MyBigAdventure&trade; wishes to promote a pro-travel mindset, and when traveling you'll need to get to the destination, sleep somewhere, eat, and do fun things when you are there.  What better way of marrying your education about a specific venue and learning about support services for that venue than from MyBigAdventure&trade; and Google&trade;!
<p>
MyBigAdventure&trade; will donate a portion of its ad revenue to <a href="javascript:myPopup1('http://www.mercycorps.org')">Mercy Corps</a>.
<p>
<img src="Graphics/mercycorps.jpg">
<p>
Mercy Corps is currently focusing a good portion of its attention and resources on the ongoing Tsunami Relief Effort.  Over 200 Mercy Corps staff are on the ground in Southern Asia, helping nearly 400,000 survivors.
<p>
Here is Mercy Corps' Mission Statement:
<p>
"Mercy Corps exists to alleviate suffering, poverty, and oppression by helping people build secure, productive, and just communities. Since 1979, Mercy Corps has provided more than $710 million in assistance to 76 nations. Mercy Corps is known nationally and internationally for its quick-response, high-impact programs, which include projects in emergency relief, sustainable community development, and civil society initiatives. Mercy Corps is committed to long-term community-based efforts that help people help themselves. With headquarters in the United States and Scotland, Mercy Corps is an international family of humanitarian agencies that reaches more than five million people each year."
<p>
<img src="Graphics/charitynavigator.jpg">
<p>
Click <a href="javascript:myPopup2('http://www.charitynavigator.org/index.cfm/bay/search.summary/orgid/4078.htm')">here</a> to learn more about Mercy Corps, as rated by <a href="javascript:myPopup3('http://www.charitynavigator.org')">Charity Navigator</a>, an non-profit organization who doesn't accept contributions from those charities (over 3700) they evaluate.
<p>
Below is one of their bar charts comparing Mercy Corps to other charities sharing the same mission.  As you can see, they rate high in all three categories, namely, organizational efficiency, organizational capacity, and overall rating.  Mercy Corps is a good, solid charity who is doing good work, that's why I picked them.
